Land Acquisition process under Act No.1 of 1894 shall be deemed to have lapsed in certain cases.--(1) Notwithstanding anything contained in this Act, in any case of land acquisition proceedings initiated under the Land Acquisition Act, 1894,--
(a) where no award under Section 11 of the said Land Acquisition Act has been made,
then, all the provisions of this Act relating to the determination of compensation shall apply;

There is no quarrel that under New Act, the determination of compensation would be at various stages viz.,
(i) at the level of Collector (Section 23 & 28);
 (ii) by the Authority (Section 64 & 69);
 (iii) at the instance of interested persons, who failed to approach the Collector under Section 64 for seeking reference (Section 73);
(iv) appeal to the High Court (Section 74).

Resultantly, the irresistible conclusion would be that the impugned order dated 16.09.2019 as well as the Award of even date are result of failure to exercise jurisdiction in the lis, by ld. ADJ;
hence, not legally sustainable and the question posed in Para 8 is answered accordingly.
